# Pigeon — Cline Rules

## Project
iOS BLE mesh messenger. Encrypted text over Bluetooth between iPhones. No internet/server. Curve25519 + AES-256-GCM E2E encryption. Each device is both BLE Central and Peripheral.

## Build
cd Pigeon && xcodebuild -scheme Pigeon -destination 'platform=iOS Simulator,name=iPhone 17 Pro' build

## Stack
Swift 5.9+, SwiftUI, iOS 26.0+, CoreBluetooth, CryptoKit, SwiftData. Zero deps. @Observable MVVM.

## CRITICAL: Concurrency
SWIFT_DEFAULT_ACTOR_ISOLATION = MainActor. ALL types @MainActor by default. DTOs must be `nonisolated Sendable`. MeshRouter is an `actor`. BLEManager is NSObject on DispatchQueue.

## Architecture
- AppCoordinator: @Observable @MainActor hub. Injected via .environment(coordinator)
- BLEManager: NSObject, dual Central+Peripheral on bleQueue. DO NOT make properties private (extensions in other files need access)
- MeshRouter: actor with outbound queue, forwarding store, dedup cache
- PigeonStore: @MainActor SwiftData facade. Maps DTO structs ↔ @Model classes
- CryptoManager: nonisolated struct, stateless encrypt/decrypt

## Two-Layer Models
DTOs (Message, Peer, Conversation) = nonisolated Codable Sendable structs in Models/
@Model classes (StoredMessage, StoredConversation, StoredPeer) = SwiftData in Persistence/
PigeonStore maps between them. NEVER merge these layers.

## Colors
PigeonTheme enum. Background #0A0A0A, accent #8B5CF6, outgoing bubble #7C3AED. Never hardcode.

## Do NOT Build
Group chats, voice/media, read receipts, cloud, LoRa, web/Android.
